      "Signal 3 — AI Drug Discovery + Refractory Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia ALL + STAT5 Oncogenic Hyperactivation + Targeted Hyperactivation Strategy / Rationale for targeted hyperactivation of oncogenic STAT5-signaling in acute lymphoblastic leukemia: GSE312311 (score 6, n=10, Homo sapiens, Genome binding/occupancy profiling by high throughput sequencing [ATAC-seq], pdat 2026/09/18 = 4 days ago, raw BW files, watcher query 'tumor metabolism single-cell' [query-routing artifact]) is the FRESHEST NOVEL STAT5-targeted-hyperactivation / oncogene-supra-addiction / ALL-refractory transcriptomic atlas in the entire 2026-09-22 hits.jsonl. STAT5 (Signal-Transducer-and-Activator-of-Transcription-5, STAT5A + STAT5B on chromosome-17q21.2, ~786-amino-acids, phosphorylated-at-Y694/Y699) is a canonical-oncogenic-transcription-factor with constitutive-activation-in-many-leukemias including BCR-ABL+ Philadelphia-chromosome-positive ALL (~25%-of-adult-ALL + ~3%-of-pediatric-ALL), T-ALL (~10-15%-of-pediatric-ALL), and FLT3-ITD-AML. Direct-STAT5-inhibition-is-challenging (SH2-domain-pocket-not-very-druggable + DNA-binding-domain-not-druggable). The KEY paradigm-shift-of-targeted-hyperactivation-of-oncogenic-STAT5: rather than inhibiting STAT5, controlled-hyperactivation-pushes-leukemic-cells-into-apoptosis-via-oncogene-supra-addiction ('oncogenic-shock' — where-cancer-cells-become-dependent-on-high-levels-of-oncogenic-signaling-and-further-increases-trigger-cell-death-via-imbalanced-pro-survival-vs-pro-apoptotic-signaling). ATAC-seq-reveals-chromatin-accessibility-changes-associated-with-STAT5-hyperactivation-providing-rationale-for-targeted-STAT5-agonist-development.",
